   "Barclays estimates the value of TPU compute clusters at $35B per GW, significantly higher than their previous assumption of $10B-$15B, which only accounted for chips and networking.",
   "The new valuation model incorporates system architecture and other components, aligning with the $63B aggregate value of a recently announced AI Compute Capacity SPV for a 1.7GW buildout.",
   "The firm remains Overweight on AVGO, raising CY27 AI revenue estimates to ~$205B (vs. Bloomberg consensus of ~$138B) and CY28 AI revenue to ~$410B (vs. consensus of ~$256B).",
   "TPU compute clusters are priced at a ~13% discount to NVDA's Vera Rubin AI systems, suggesting strong appetite for ASICs despite the narrowing price gap.",
   "Credit research views the impact on AVGO credit quality as negligible, noting that accelerating earnings and cash flow absorb the leverage impact of backstops.",
   "Supply technicals remain a risk, with Broadcom planning to deploy 20GW through the XPV platform through 2028, potentially leading to issuance exceeding $500B.",
   "Broadcom has reduced the backstop percentage on its XPV platform deals from 85% in the first transaction to 72.5% in the most recent, with expectations for further declines."
