  "title": "Security Software: Elevated Threats Support Ongoing Cybersecurity Demand: Previewing CHKP, FROG, QLYS, RPD, CLBT",
  "type": "equity_research",
  "priority": "medium",
  "published": "2026-10-29",
  "insights": [
   "Rising critical vulnerabilities, accelerated by AI-driven discovery, are driving cybersecurity spending from an IT concern to a board-level business continuity priority.",
   "Enterprises are increasingly migrating off legacy Network Security, Endpoint, and Identity environments, with security budgets expected to accelerate into 2027.",
   "Typical sales cycles of 6-12 months suggest that the upside from increased threat urgency will be more visible in 4Q26 and 2027 rather than 3Q26 results.",
   "Vendors with exposure to next-gen platforms (CRWD, PANW), software supply chain governance (FROG), identity platforms (OKTA, SAIL, PANW), and exposure management (TENB, QLYS) are best positioned.",
   "Investor focus for upcoming earnings will center on forward-looking demand indicators, pipeline conversion, and early 2027 budget signals.",
   "JPM remains Overweight FROG and CLBT, Neutral CHKP and QLYS, and Underweight RPD."
